"typeCode":"IND","group":"ind","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Independent Study","typeCode":"IND","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":[]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"GWS 393","subject":"GWS","number":"393","title":"Policing Latinx Immigrant Communities","creditHours":"3 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":["1US"],"degreeAttributes":"Cultural Studies - US Minority course.","scheduleNote":"","info":"","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"78716","code":"DVB","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["M","W"],"start":720,"end":800,"location":"111 Gregory Hall","instructors":["Vergara Bracamontes, D"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"GWS 395","subject":"GWS","number":"395","title":"Intermediate Topics GWS","creditHours":"3 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Approved for letter and S/U grading. May be repeated in the same term to a maximum of 9 hours; may be repeated in separate terms to a maximum of 12 hours.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"51239","code":"EK","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["T","R"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"44 English Building","instructors":["Kramer, E"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"Topic: Meets with ANTH 352 (CRN: 75699), Language and Gender. The relationship between language and gender is complex, contentious, and often misunderstood. In this course, we explore the many connections between language and gender. Topics include what gender is and how it is socially and linguistically constituted; real and perceived differences — grammatical, phonological, conversational — in how men and women speak; how the ways we talk about gender shape the ways we think about gender; and how all of these things vary cross-culturally and cross-linguistically. This course focuses on the role of language in constructing and sustaining gender in different societies around the world. We will examine linguistic mechanisms of creating gender divisions and stereotypes, as well as remedying gender-related inequality. Overall, the course aims to challenge our received notions of what gender is and how language and gender are interconnected. Among the topics covered are: institutional language and power; gender identity and language use; ideologies of gender and language; cultural definitions of “masculinity” and “femininity” and their relationship to language use; language and desire; and the social construction of gender identities through linguistic performance."}]},{"id":"GWS 399","subject":"GWS","number":"399","title":"GWS Internship","creditHours":"3 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Approved for Letter and S/U grading. Prerequisite: GWS major or minor; junior or senior standing and completion of six hours of coursework in GWS, or consent of the instructor.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"68616","code":"MK","typeCode":"INT","group":"int","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Internship","typeCode":"INT","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":["Khan, M"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"GWS 409","subject":"GWS","number":"409","title":"Women's Health","creditHours":"3 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Same as HK 409. See HK 409.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"31276","code":"A","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["T","R"],"start":750,"end":830,"location":"112 Huff Hall","instructors":["Gobin, R"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"Some seats are held for majors, but others are open to the public. Additional seats will be released on December 10. Please contact the Department with any questions."}]},{"id":"GWS 415","subject":"GWS","number":"415","title":"Africana Feminisms","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Same as AFRO 415 and AFST 420. See AFRO 415.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"62163","code":"1","typeCode":"ONL","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Online","typeCode":"ONL","days":["F"],"start":540,"end":710,"location":"n.a.","instructors":["Harrison, F"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null},{"crn":"62184","code":"G1","typeCode":"ONL","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Online","typeCode":"ONL","days":["F"],"start":540,"end":710,"location":"n.a.","instructors":["Harrison, F"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"GWS 432","subject":"GWS","number":"432","title":"Gender Communication","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Same as CMN 432. See CMN 432.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"37087","code":"1","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["T","R"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"1027 Lincoln Hall","instructors":["Giorgio, G"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"GWS 435","subject":"GWS","number":"435","title":"Commodifying Difference","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Same as AAS 435, AFRO 435, LLS 435, and MACS 432. See LLS 435.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"40446","code":"G","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["T","R"],"start":840,"end":920,"location":"327 Gregory Hall","instructors":["Peoples, G"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"An interdisciplinary examination of how racial, ethnic and gender difference is negotiated through media and popular culture, and how racial, ethnic and gendered communities use cultural forms to express identity and difference. Among the theoretical questions explored in the course are the politics of representation, ethnic/racial authenticity, cultural commodification and transnational popular culture. Some of the cultural forms examined are cultural festivals/parades, ethnic/race-based beauty pageants, cinematic and televisual texts and musical forms, such as Hip-Hop and Salsa."},{"crn":"40517","code":"U","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["T","R"],"start":840,"end":920,"location":"327 Gregory Hall","instructors":["Peoples, G"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"An interdisciplinary examination of how racial, ethnic and gender difference is negotiated through media and popular culture, and h